uilding and physical premises safety, including identification and protection from hazards that can cause bodily injury such as electrical hazards, bodies of water, and vehicular traffic; and     (7) Handling, storing, and disposing of hazardous materials including compliance with ?746.3425 of this chapter (relating to Must caregivers wear gloves when handling blood or bodily fluids containing blood?).","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026494700","violation_type_title":"Documented Annual Training Area - 24 Hours Required (26 TAC §746.1309(a))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392315-i20250317-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2207-c-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392315-i20250317","date":"2025-03-17","original_code":"746.2207(c)(4)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-26","finding":"Screen Time Activities - Not Used During Eating or Rest Times: Five school aged children were observed on cell phones and tablet watching videos/shows as they were getting ready for nap time. The content being viewed by children was not age appropriate or related to the operations planned activities. A child was observed playing a game called Roblox, Two children were observed watching videos on You Tube and two other children were observed watching a show called Squid Games.         Note: This was addressed with the staff and the electronics were removed and stored and away.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026414845","violation_type_title":"Screen Time Activities - Not Used During Eating or Rest Times (26 TAC §746.2207(c)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392315-i20250317-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1605-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392315-i20250317","date":"2025-03-17","original_code":"746.1605(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-